<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dardanians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dardani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dardanians were an ancient people of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, living in the region of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>. Warlike northern neighbours of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, they raided it repeatedly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a>, and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-ii-nicator">Demetrius II</a> died around 229 BCE after a defeat by them. Under Roman rule their territory formed the region of Dardania.</p></div>
